{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 36, :comments ["<b>Nevertheless a spring or cistern, a gathering of waters.</b> Those attached to the ground do not receive impurity. And further you have to learn: <b>it shall be pure</b> — one who immerses in them becomes pure from his impurity." "<b>And one who touches their carcass shall become impure.</b> Even if he is inside a spring or cistern and touches their impurity, he becomes impure — so that you not say a fortiori: if it purifies the impure from their impurity, a fortiori it should preserve the pure from becoming impure. Therefore it is stated: וְנֹגֵעַ בְּנִבְלָתָם יִטְמָא (Nedarim 77a)."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:05:57.148195011Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}